quiet.md: App::hide_cursor_until_mouse_moves

Upstream dropped CursorStyle::None and hides the pointer itself on typing
(CursorHideMode). The app hides it where it decides to (typing in the editor
and fields, an idle image viewer) and turns CursorHideMode off, so expose the
platform call it used through CursorStyle::None.

diff --git a/crates/gpui/src/app.rs b/crates/gpui/src/app.rs
index 64a79c7942132b69d9f1d76bb5ecbbcbece9a51a..12e4690e6023321db495f7d2878a07494c13350a 100644
--- a/crates/gpui/src/app.rs
+++ b/crates/gpui/src/app.rs
@@ -1398,6 +1398,12 @@ impl App {
         self.cursor_hide_mode = mode;
     }
 
+    /// quiet.md: hide the mouse cursor until the mouse next moves (what
+    /// [`CursorHideMode`] does on typing), for apps that decide when.
+    pub fn hide_cursor_until_mouse_moves(&self) {
+        self.platform.hide_cursor_until_mouse_moves();
+    }
+
